  <data name="AlternateExplainer" xml:space="preserve"><value>A single-rest week rests the chosen day; a full week rests Saturday and Sunday. When a weekend make-up day cuts it to one rest day, the next week is a full week; with two, the next week is single-rest, and the alternation continues. A weekend with no rest flips as planned, and a mid-week holiday does not change the alternation. Changing this week's choice makes this week the new reference, with statutory make-up days still taking priority; changing anything else keeps the old reference.</value></data>
